{
  "apiVersion": "v1",
  "kind": "List",
  "metadata": {
    "annotations": {
      "uptimebuyer.dev/note": "Reference egress policy (M14, configuration only, NOT_RUN: never applied to a cluster). Default deny; only the kite-broker may reach the internet (443, private ranges excluded) and it should additionally sit behind an egress gateway allow-listing the Kite and merchant endpoints by name. The API reaches only DNS, PostgreSQL and the identity provider (203.0.113.0/24 is a documentation placeholder for the IdP's published range). The worker and sensor gateway reach only DNS and PostgreSQL. Operations ports accept only the monitoring namespace. The broker accepts signed references only on a unix socket, which cannot cross pods: a cluster deployment needs either a node-local socket (broker and its clients scheduled on the same node, each in its own pod and service account) or an mTLS transport for the same reference-only protocol, which is not implemented (residual risk). No TCP ingress reaches the broker."
    }
  },
  "items": [
